This looks like late 2023. The fed funds rate of 5.33 matches the 5.25–5.50 target range, which was in place from July 2023 to September 2024. A 1-month equity return of +9.1% and a 20y+ Treasury return of +9.9% fit November 2023, when yields fell sharply. The 10-year yield at 4.27 also fits the end of November 2023, when it was about 4.37, or possibly a December reading.

Some figures give pause. The 3-month change in the 10-year yield is +0.18, which suggests the yield was about 4.09 three months earlier, and end of August 2023 was around 4.09, so that fits. The 2-year yield was 4.64 at the end of November 2023 and the 12-month change of +0.26 fits, since it was about 4.3 in November 2022. Headline CPI of 3.23 is close to the October 2023 reading of 3.2%, and core CPI of 4.02 is close to 4.0%. The unemployment rate of 3.9% matches October 2023. VIX at 12.98 fits the end of November 2023 or December. This all points to November 2023.

